{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronShapeBridge","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronShapeBridge","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.BlochWignerLobachevsky","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.hessian_det_eq_one_ofShape","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.hessian_det_eq_one_ofShape","kind":"theorem","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/IdealTetrahedronShapeBridge.lean#L103-L111","doc":"**The determinant is exactly `1` at every shape.**  The `det H = 1`\nrigidity, transported the same way — it does not degenerate anywhere in the\nupper half plane. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.hessian_neg_definite_ofShape","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.hessian_neg_definite_ofShape","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/IdealTetrahedronShapeBridge.lean#L89-L101","doc":"**The concavity result, transported to shape coordinates.**\n\nThe cotangent Hessian is negative definite at the tetrahedron of *every* shape\n`z` in the upper half plane — in particular at a substrate shape parameter `z_q`,\nonce `Im z_q > 0` is supplied.  No new mathematics: `ofShape` plus\n`hessian_neg_definite`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.AngleTriple.ofShape_γ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.AngleTriple.ofShape_γ","kind":"theorem","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/IdealTetrahedronShapeBridge.lean#L86-L87","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.AngleTriple.ofShape_β","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.AngleTriple.ofShape_β","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/IdealTetrahedronShapeBridge.lean#L83-L84","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.AngleTriple.ofShape_α","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.AngleTriple.ofShape_α","kind":"theorem","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/IdealTetrahedronShapeBridge.lean#L80-L81","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.AngleTriple.ofShape","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.AngleTriple.ofShape","kind":"def","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/IdealTetrahedronShapeBridge.lean#L65-L78","doc":"**The shape parameter of an ideal tetrahedron is an `AngleTriple`.**\n\nFor `Im z > 0`, the dihedral angles `(arg z, arg(1/(1−z)), arg(1−1/z))` are\npositive and sum to `π` — exactly the `AngleTriple` data.  Every hypothesis is\ndischarged by a theorem that already existed; what was missing was the\nobservation that the two files describe the same object. ","signatureChunk":0}]}